When I invoke dxterm, the TERM variable is set to vt300. The following
escape codes work for this case:

#   Make header of dec-window hostname:user current directory
                echo "\033]21;$dir\033\ "
#   Make icon hostname:user current directory
                echo "\033]2L;$dir\033\ "

*** $dir variable is what you want to put in the window title,
	e.g. (using ksh) dir="[`hostname | cut -f 1 -d '.'`:`whoami`] $PWD"
	puts hostname, user and current working directory as title.

For xterm windows, the TERM variable is set to xterm. The following
escape codes work for this case:

#   Make header of xterm hostname:user current directory
                echo "\033]2;$dir\\07"
#   Make icon hostname:user current directory
                echo "\033]1;$dir\\07"

