In article <1995Oct16.150101.9292@ais.com>, goutham@ais.com wrote:

>I am running OSF/1(ver. 2.0) on an ALPHA System and the system fails
>to boot with the message: "vm_swap_init: /sbin/swapdefault swap device not
>found - swap over commitment mode". Any help is greatly appreciated.

This message gets shown when you don't have the file necessary to get the
computer to swap in eager mode.  You are in the deferred or lazy swap
mode, which tends to reserve a lot less swap space.  We run like this all
the time.

This error should not keep the computer from booting.  There is something
else wrong, somewhere.

